WEBVTT

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.280
I'm late!

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.030
I'm late. I'm late. I'm late!

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.530
I am <i>so</i> late...

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.950
I can't get my eyebrows right.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.040
Too crowded...

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.330
I can't help it.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:21.450
If you squeeze in a bit more...

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.710
Sonata, you're in my way.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.080
<i>You're</i> in <i>mine</i>.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.420
I don't want to miss breakfast.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:31.970
Grumbly, if you keep scrubbing
you'll make yourself look plainer.

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:33.220
I do <i>not</i> look plain!

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:35.720
Grumbly's gonna rumble me!

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:37.140
Shut up already!

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:42.520
Chef Papa! Your breakfasts are amazing!

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:43.350
I'll have seconds!

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.270
Sonata, too!

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.830
Looks like you've gotten used to life here.

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:00.870
Takamina-san!

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.330
Good morning!

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:03.410
Morning!

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:04.960
Start the day with a good breakfast!

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.500
Right!

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:09.540
Extra helpings.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:11.500
No more?

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:12.670
I'm sorry.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:14.840
Everyone has such big appetites.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:15.590
See?

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:17.510
Extra helpings.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.100
Only had five.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.600
Nowhere near enough.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.850
I-I'll make more! Right away!

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.180
More please.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:22.850
More rice...

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:29.310
<i>It's been a month since we came to Akibastar and started living together as understudies.</i>

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:34.150
<i>By now, we've more or less developed a routine.</i>

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:35.900
No running allowed.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:37.160
This is a walking race.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:37.780
Okay!

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:42.240
<i>After breakfast, we head to the dorm's practice room.</i>

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:45.910
<i>In order to get the position
diagonally behind Ushiyama-sensei,</i>

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:50.340
<i>where we can observe his movements the best,</i>

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.800
<i>we all race to be the first one there.</i>

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:55.840
Good morning!

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:00.470
Ushiyama-sensei?

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:01.510
He's not here.

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:02.600
What are you up to?

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:05.310
Tsubasa-san.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:06.770
You don't have lessons today.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:09.560
It's your monthly recreational day.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:12.360
This applies to both you and the successors.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.900
What?

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.320
Oh yeah...

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.280
I completely forgot.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.910
Then let's practice on our own!

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:21.490
Good idea!

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:22.240
Isn't it?

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.580
Okay!

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:26.540
I like that! Nice idea!

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:27.410
Are you sure?

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:28.830
Huh?

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:31.750
00 members' lives are scheduled down to the minute.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:35.000
How you use your time is very important.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:41.550
The ability to make the most of your days off will greatly impact your futures.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:46.020
Ready, set, here we go!

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.060
AKB0048!

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:05.120
Even if you reach out your hand,

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:11.710
you won't be able to reach it yet.

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:17.300
Our dreams still lie

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:22.890
much, much further in the distance.

